.vercel
# Every .env variant is a secret — except the committed template. `vercel env
# pull` appends a bare `.env*`, which would swallow .env.example too; the
# negation is what keeps the setup docs' reference file in the repo.
.env*
!.env.example
# The owner's local seed script — body metrics, targets and weigh-in history.
# PRD § P7: "no personal metrics in git history, ever". Recipes, workouts and
# the weekly template are committed under src/lib/seed/ because they are food,
# exercises and routine; only the profile row and the weigh-ins are personal,
# and they live here. `scripts/seed-local.example.ts` is the committed template,
# carrying the demo persona's invented figures — see README → Seeding.
#
# Not a `scripts/*.local.ts` glob: one named file, so a future script cannot
# fall into the ignore by accident and go missing from a review.
scripts/seed-local.ts

